        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en">The described plant Leibstadt (CH) started commercial operation at the end of 1984. It belongs to the 1000 MW class (net installed capacity has been upgraded in steps from the original 990 MW to 1165 MW at the end of 1999). It has a GE (USA) designed primary circuit, a Mark III containment, and a cooling tower. This module can be assumed to be representative for the boiling water reactors of the same class in USA.\n\n# Included processes\nThe module includes materials, energy and transport requirements used for construction of the plant. Land-use is included with the assumption of 40 years operation. Disposal of non-contaminated material from dismantling is also included, whereas contaminated materials are attributed to the operation.</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
        </technology>
